Naledi: [her eyes going straight to the Roller] You brought it.
Naledi: I watched you from here yesterday. You made one trip to the river and came back with — how much does that hold?
Hippo: Ninety litres.
Naledi: [quietly] Ninety litres.
Naledi: I made four trips yesterday. Each one nearly twenty litres on my head.
Naledi: Hippo. Can I ask you something?
- Of course.
    Hippo: Of course. Ask.
    jump naledi_quest_offer_direct_ask/
- What is it?
    Hippo: What is it?
    jump naledi_quest_offer_direct_ask/